/P <<
/ActualText (Before we talk about the stock market\054 I want you to understand what builds wealth\056 When you buy something\054 you can purchase either an asset or a liability\056 When you buy a liability\054 that purchase takes money out of your bank account repetitively\056 Say\054 for example\054 you buy a house\056 Now\054 you have to pay for your bills\054 possibly your mortgage\054 utility issues\054 paint\054 and more\056 This house is a liability because it takes money out of your pocket after you buy it\056 On the other hand\054 if you buy a house and rent it out to somebody\054 it is an asset as long as the money you take in covers your expenses\056 When you make money from buying something that pays you back over time\054 you have an asset\041 I want you to make asset your new favorite word\054 because purchasing assets and minimizing liabilities is the key to growing your wealth\056)
/MCID 1
>> BDC
