/P <<
/ActualText (When you buy stocks\054 you go through brokerages to get them\056 These companies connect to the big\055name exchanges you hear about all over Wall Street\056 We will talk about brokers later\054 but you should remember one thing about these corporations\072 they all have to listen to the SEC\056 The SEC is the U\056S\056 Security and Exchange Commission\054 an independent federal agency created by the Securities Exchange Act of 1934\056\271 The SEC regulates the whole stock market\054 and they are important because they set all the rules of trading\056 You need to remember a few of the SEC\220s rules when you are investing or else you risk a frozen brokerage account or cash liquidity issues\056 Brokers usually inform you about the most important SEC rules right before you break them\054 so you do not have to worry too much about actually researching them\056 With that said\054 there are two SEC\055identified circumstances that many people have trouble with\056)
/MCID 1
