/P <<
/ActualText (To save for college\054 some parents open UGMA or UTMA accounts for their children when they are still young\056 These parents can invest their own money into assets that will grow as their children grow up\056 As we talked about earlier\054 these accounts only offer tax advantages up to the first few thousand dollars in annual gains\054 gains that are taxed at the minor\220s capital gains tax rate which is almost always lower than the custodian\220s tax rate since your child rarely outearns you in their teenage years\056 Afterwards\054 these accounts act as normal brokerage accounts used solely for the benefit of the child\056 Any money withdrawn from the account must be spent on something that directly benefits the account\220s minor\056\271 Additionally\054 the minor can spend the money in the account on anything once they mature and receive ownership of the account\056\262 These accounts are called Universal \215Gifts\216 and Universal \215Transfers\216 to Minors Acts\056 Parents who put money in these accounts are giving their children money down the road\056 Moreover\054 you cannot change the beneficiary of a UGMA or UTMA account\056\263)
/MCID 2
>> BDC
