/P <<
/ActualText (Commodities and currencies are generally tougher markets to profit from compared to stocks and corporate bonds\056 Some traders make consistent profits by using technical analysis to actively manage commodity and \050non\055crypto\051 currency portfolios\054 but these traders generally see less volatility and realize lower percent gains than nine\055to\055noon traders \050see Part Two\051\056 Some active foreign exchange currency traders make up for low volatilities by using leveraged debt to increase their position stakes\054 but we already talked about why you should avoid trading on margin earlier\056 With that said\054 you can make strong medium\055term gains if you think a certain commodity industry will significantly change in the near\055term\056 For example\054 a horrendous hurricane in Florida may increase FCOJ\055A futures prices \050we will talk about what this means soon\051\056 Perhaps you notice gas prices getting especially low and see potential upside in crude oil\056 Alternatively\054 you can use currency markets to profit from your overall knowledge of worldwide political issues and country\055specific news as currencies quickly change value compared to one another\056)
/MCID 1
