/ActualText (Call options give you the right to purchase an underlying asset by a specified date at the strike price\056 When you buy calls or puts\054 your initial investment is nonrefundable\056 An option premium will cost more if the strike price is closer to the spot price\056\263 You will also pay more for options with later expiration dates since the underlying asset has more time to reach the strike price\056 Lastly\054 the cost to buy an option may increase as the volatility of the underlying asset increases\056\263)
/MCID 2
