/ActualText (When a company decides to split its stock\054 its board of directors picks a split ratio\056 In a normal\054 forward stock split\054 a company divides its stock price by the split ratio while simultaneously multiplying the number of shares outstanding by the split ratio in shareholder accounts \050for more information\054 see stock registrars in Chapter 37\051\056 All existing shareholders have their position size multiplied by the split ratio while the price of each share decreases by the same factor to maintain the same overall value\056)
/MCID 3
>> BDC
