/ActualText (Moving averages are moving because they drop the last data point from a series and add a new one once available\056 Therefore\054 to continue our example\054 we drop the oldest \04412 price from the five\055period moving average and replace it with the next period\220s price\056\271 The three most\055used averages are the 50\054 100\054 and 200 moving averages\056\262 Since these are popular\054 many other investors will look at these price levels and consider them as support and resistance levels just like you\056 Because these levels are mostly psychological\054 these averages serve as support and resistance levels throughout all time frames\056 With that said\054 longer measurement intervals produce stronger moving averages\056\262 Here is a weekly\055candlestick chart of Tesla\054 Inc\056 with all three major moving averages\072)
/MCID 6
