/P <<
/ActualText (It is tough to predict the exact top or bottom of any stock movement\056 Nobody is perfect in financial analysis\054 and many long\055term prices average out over time\056 However\054 you can get optimal fill prices by using trendlines and indicators\056 These rarely form perfect setups on their own\054 but they present compelling opportunities when used together to identify trends\056 Some indicators work better than others depending on the stock you are trading\054 whereas other assets rely more on trendlines\056 Try out different indicators and trendlines on stocks to find ones that work in a given situation\056 All of the indicators you have learned about work well in different analysis situations\056 You may get better results with an indicator or perhaps find a stronger trendline when you change the time frame of a stock chart\056 Most indicators look radically different as you change from hourly to weekly candlesticks\056 As you find the asset\055management time commitment that suits you\054 you will naturally figure out which indicators and trendlines work best alongside your trading strategy\056 All indicators eventually return to normalcy\056)
/MCID 1
