/P <<
/ActualText (You can never be 100 percent sure on any stock pick\056 So\054 your whole portfolio should determine your success rather than a few stocks\056\271 With a wider range of assets\054 you give yourself many more chances to succeed while you slowly weed out underperforming investments\056 Give your losing stocks time to play out if they have a strong underlying setup\054 business plan\054 etc\056 before you cut them from your portfolio\056 Simultaneously\054 let your winners run until you think they have no steam left\056 Remember that the risk with any investment is that the entire company goes bankrupt and the stock goes to \0440\056 Companies with long histories might be less likely to go bankrupt\054 but you still do not want to let one stock take too much of your portfolio\056 By diversifying\054 you minimize the impact individual downtrends will have on your portfolio\056)
/MCID 4
>> BDC
