/ActualText (I started learning about our economy on my own a few months before I left my year\055long job at Subway in the latter part of my sophomore year\056 Inspired by my research\054 I started trading stocks after school\056 Once summer came along\054 I started actively trading every weekday\056 In my first few weeks of trading with my saved Subway money\054 my profits quickly taught me the earning power of the stock market\073 I made much more trading stocks than I ever thought possible\056 I continued trading throughout the summer partially for the money but also because I loved every market morning and the nine\055to\055noon workday\056 However\054 my fun started approaching an end as the school year started\054 and I realized that I could not trade the opening bell in second period\056 Thus\054 I started looking for other ways to keep growing\056 I started investigating cryptocurrencies and \042mining\042 with computers while on a family trip\056 I planned and built my first computer the Christmas prior\054 and this technical background helped me understand some of the baseline consensus processes behind cryptocurrencies\056 I researched hundreds of cryptocurrencies of all prices and market sectors before junior year\056 The more I watched smaller\054 volatile currencies\054 the more I saw the same patterns I traded in the stock market\056 Once school)
/MCID 2
